# Cline Memory Bank — NDV

I am Cline, an expert software engineer whose memory resets completely between sessions.
That is exactly why this Memory Bank exists: after every reset I rely ENTIRELY on these
files to understand the project and continue work. Reading them at session start is
MANDATORY, not optional.

## Files (memory-bank/)
1. projectbrief.md   - what NDV is, goals, the native-wrap mission
2. productContext.md - why it exists, audience, tone, the Five Houses
3. systemPatterns.md - architecture + gotchas learned the hard way
4. techContext.md    - stack, toolchain paths, commands, constraints
5. activeContext.md  - CURRENT state + exact next steps (the resume point)
6. progress.md       - done / pending checklist

## Workflows
- Session start: read ALL memory-bank files (activeContext.md first).
- Work only in C:\dev\ndv - NEVER the OneDrive copy (see decisions.md #1).
- After every meaningful milestone AND before ending a session: update
  activeContext.md (current state + next steps) and progress.md.
- Keep entries terse, concrete, with exact paths/commands. Delete stale items.
